< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"status","title":"REAPER status","description":"Whether Kumi's bridge in REAPER is connected: the REAPER and bridge versions, the open project, and whether REAPER is busy (a dialog, a render). With several REAPER instances running, pass pid or resource from discover.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The REAPER process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The REAPER resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"discover","title":"Find running REAPER","description":"Every running REAPER with Kumi's bridge: process id, port, resource folder, versions, open project, and whether it answers. Use it when status reports none, or to choose among several.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"read","title":"Read REAPER","description":"Rows of one kind from the open REAPER project, a page at a time: {items, nextCursor?, epoch}. Pass parent (a row's ref) to read what is inside it, such as a track's items or an FX's parameters; pass the previous page's nextCursor as cursor for the next page. Or pass ref alone for the one object it names. Refs hold until the epoch changes. With several REAPER instances running, pass pid or resource from discover.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The REAPER process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The REAPER resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["project","track","item","take","fx","param","send","marker","region","note","event","envelope","point","autoitem","call"],"description":"What to read in REAPER."},"parent":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of what the rows are in: a track for its items or sends, an FX for its parameters."},"ref":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of one object to read instead of a page of rows."},"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"The nextCursor an earlier page gave, unchanged."},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":200,"description":"Rows in a page (50 by default)."},"epoch":{"type":"string","description":"The epoch of the answer the ref, parent or cursor came from. If the project in the tab has changed since, the call is refused as stale instead of reading the other project."},"fn":{"type":"string","description":"For kind call: a REAPER API function that only reads, by name."},"args":{"type":["array","object"],"description":"For kind call: its arguments, in order or by the SDK's names; tracks, items, takes and envelopes as refs."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"snapshot","title":"REAPER snapshot","description":"The open REAPER project on one screen: {epoch, project, transport, tracks, selection, markers?}. What is too big to include is named under truncated, to read with `read`.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The REAPER process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The REAPER resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"focus","title":"REAPER focus","description":"What the producer is looking at in REAPER: {epoch, view, selection, transport, changed}. Cheap enough to poll about every 150 ms; read again only when changed moves.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The REAPER process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The REAPER resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"focus_body","title":"REAPER view","description":"What REAPER shows in one of its views, ready to draw: pass kind, and ref (the take, track or pattern it is about) or window (the range to show) where the kind takes them. Long ones come in pages: pass the nextCursor as cursor.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The REAPER process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The REAPER resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["arrange","midi","fx","routing","mixer"],"description":"Which view."},"ref":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of what the view is about."},"around":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of a track to centre the first page of tracks on (the arrange view): the page starts half a page above it, and says where in `from`."},"window":{"type":"object","properties":{"from":{"type":"number"},"to":{"type":"number"}},"required":["from","to"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The range to show, in the view's own units."},"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"The nextCursor an earlier page gave, unchanged."},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":200,"description":"Rows in a page."},"epoch":{"type":"string","description":"The epoch of the answer the ref, parent or cursor came from. If the project in the tab has changed since, the call is refused as stale instead of reading the other project."}},"required":["kind"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"change_preview","title":"Preview a REAPER change","description":"What one change would do in REAPER, without making it: {transactionId, confirmation, prior, display, target, epoch}. Apply it with change_apply.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The REAPER process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The REAPER resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"kind":{"type":"string","description":"The change kind."},"input":{"type":"object","description":"What the kind takes."},"epoch":{"type":"string","description":"The epoch the refs in input came from."}},"required":["kind","input"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"change_apply","title":"Apply a REAPER change","description":"Makes a previewed change in REAPER, as one named step of REAPER's undo. The same idempotencyKey again returns the first answer and changes nothing. state is applied, or uncertain when REAPER didn't answer.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"transactionId":{"type":"string"},"confirmation":{"type":"string","description":"The confirmation change_preview gave."},"idempotencyKey":{"type":"string"},"title":{"type":"string","description":"The change's name in REAPER's undo history."}},"required":["transactionId","confirmation","idempotencyKey"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"change_undo","title":"Undo a REAPER change","description":"Takes a change back as a new named step in REAPER: exactly what it changed is put back. Refused (code changed) if those values changed since, unless discard.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"transactionId":{"type":"string"},"confirmation":{"const":"undo"},"idempotencyKey":{"type":"string"},"discard":{"type":"boolean","description":"Put the values back even if they changed since."}},"required":["transactionId","confirmation","idempotencyKey"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"transport_stop","title":"Stop REAPER","description":"Stops REAPER's playback and recording at once.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The REAPER process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The REAPER resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"transport_play","title":"Play REAPER","description":"Starts REAPER's playback from where it is, or (Renoise) from sequence (a slot, from 1) and line.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The REAPER process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The REAPER resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"sequence":{"type":"integer","minimum":1},"line":{"type":"integer","minimum":1},"epoch":{"type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"cursor_set","title":"Move REAPER's cursor","description":"Moves REAPER's edit cursor to positionBeats (quarter notes from the start) or position (seconds); the play position follows while it plays.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The REAPER process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The REAPER resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"positionBeats":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"position":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"epoch":{"type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"undo_step_begin","title":"Begin one REAPER undo step","description":"Opens one step of REAPER's undo around the changes that follow, where REAPER gives one: {stepId}. Close it with undo_step_end.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"label":{"type":"string"}},"required":["label"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"undo_step_end","title":"End the REAPER undo step","description":"Closes the step undo_step_begin opened; label names it in REAPER's undo by what it did.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"stepId":{"type":"string"},"label":{"type":"string","maxLength":200}},"required":["stepId"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"change_release","title":"Forget changes","description":"Changes that won't be undone any more: the host forgets them (at most 64 at a time).","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"transactionIds":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1,"maxItems":64}},"required":["transactionIds"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"project_save","title":"Save the REAPER project","description":"Saves the open REAPER project where it is, or as its next version (version: true). A project never saved is saved only under path, a .rpp inside the folder REAPER saves projects in, and never over a file.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The REAPER process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The REAPER resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"version":{"type":"boolean"},"path":{"type":"string"},"epoch":{"type":"string","description":"The epoch of the answer the project was read in: if the project open now is another, the save is refused as stale."}},"required":["epoch"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"track_template_save","title":"Save REAPER tracks as a template","description":"Writes tracks as a track template (.RTrackTemplate) in REAPER's TrackTemplates folder (name) or at path; never over a file unless replace.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The REAPER process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The REAPER resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"trackRefs":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1},"name":{"type":"string"},"path":{"type":"string"},"items":{"type":"boolean"},"envelopes":{"type":"boolean"},"replace":{"type":"boolean"},"epoch":{"type":"string","description":"The epoch of the answer the ref, parent or cursor came from. If the project in the tab has changed since, the call is refused as stale instead of reading the other project."}},"required":["trackRefs","epoch"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"fx_chain_save","title":"Save an FX chain file","description":"Saves a chain's FX (fxRefs: some of them, in the chain's order) as an FX chain file (.RfxChain) under name in REAPER's FXChains folder: no FX ids, no automation. A file of that name is replaced only with overwrite. A file, not the project: no step of REAPER's undo.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The REAPER process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The REAPER resource or preferences folder to use, from discover, when several run."},"ref":{"type":"string","description":"The track, take, item or container whose chain to save."},"input":{"type":"boolean","description":"The track's input FX chain."},"fxRefs":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1,"maxItems":256},"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":256,"description":"The file's name in FXChains; sub-folders as \"Vocals/Lead\"."},"overwrite":{"type":"boolean"},"epoch":{"type":"string"}},"required":["ref","name"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}}]}}
